  "body": "Replace the slice-1 probe refusal in `assets/posts/okuma-osp.cps` (#1964) with clean-room Okuma OSP probing routines. Confirm the shop target macro package (Okuma gauging `CALL OO..` macros vs skip `G31` with `VC` variables) from shop feedback or public Okuma manuals before writing code.\n\n## Requirements\n- Do not copy Fanuc Macro B variables (`#100..`, `#5061..`, `#3000`, `G10 L2`, `#5221`) from `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`. OSP controls use `VC` common variables, `V`-series system variables, `G31` skip moves, and `CALL OO..` library routines.\n- Implement `onProbe`, `onProbeMove`, `onProbeRetreat`, `onProbeGuard`, and `onProbeResult` in `okuma-osp.cps` to update `G15 H` offsets (`VZOFX`/`VZOFY`/`VZOFZ` or `CALL` cycle outputs) without starting spindle rotation or coolant.\n- Set `probeAxisInversion = true` only after verifying inverted-axis probe sign handling with unit tests (`crates/app/tests/probe_op.rs` and `crates/app/tests/probe_no_coolant.rs` patterns).\n\nDone means: `okuma-osp.cps` posts valid OSP probing routines with no Fanuc `#` variables, keeps spindle and coolant off during probe cycles, updates `G15 H` offsets, and passes probe unit tests.\n\nPart of #1959\n",
